<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="plaunotol biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260303222105">
  <Description>Plaunotol is the bioactive compound responsible for the medicinal properties found in |FRAME: TAX-431156|, a Thai medicinal plant. |FRAME: CPD-11423| is an acyclic diterpene alcohol which is formed from four isoprenoid units. |FRAME: FARNESYL-PP| and |FRAME: DELTA3-ISOPENTENYL-PP| molecules are condensed by the enzyme Geranylgeranyl pyrophosphate synthase (GGPPS). This reaction results in the formation of the product geranylgeranyldiphosphate (GGPP) |CITS: [19782428]|. This is followed by a two step monodephosphorylation of GGPP to form geranylgeraniol |CITS: [16445953]|. The final step is catalyzed by GGOH 18-hydroxylase to form |FRAME: CPD-11423|. |FRAME: CPD-11423| shows broad spectrum inhibition of acute gastric and duodenal ulcers |CITS: [15855831]|. It also helps the healing of the chronic gastric ulcers by reducing the size of ulcers, reduced secretion of gastric juice, acid and pepsin, reviewed here |CITS: [18845620]|. It also significantly helps the regeneration of mucosa. Several papers report the positive effects of |FRAME: CPD-11423| on colon cancer |CITS: [15746576]|, |CITS: [17691055]|, |CITS: [18805546]|. The purification of |FRAME: CPD-11423| is a patented procedure, the elucidation of the biosynthesis of this compound is underway and the above pathway shows the last few steps. A few of the enzymes in the precursor |FRAME: NONMEVIPP-PWY| has also been isolated, cloned and characterized |CITS: [18451506]|. Expression studies on these enzymes have shown their localization to be leaf and twig specific and absent in roots. Some of the enzyme sequences show the presence of chloroplast targeting sequences |CITS: [19782428]|.</Description>
